<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrei II of Vladimir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1222–<a href="/years/1264">1264</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Andrei Yaroslavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrei II of Vladimir (Andrei Yaroslavich) was grand prince of Vladimir from 1249 to 1252, a son of Yaroslav II and younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>. Appointed by the Mongol court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakorum">Karakorum</a>, he tried to act independently of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>; in 1252 a Mongol army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevryuy">Nevryuy</a> defeated him and he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. He later returned and held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> until his death in 1264.</p></div>
